{
  "_comment": "The battery swing (exe patch 143, docs/notes/battery-hit.md): a forward ram, authored on the stock rig (scripts/battery-hit: swing.py's keys, make_clips.py writes them) as the game plays a battery state: its player clips move the carrier's arms alone (bone mask 2), its battery clips the battery by its own offset bone. The battery's states 3 (the swing: wind-up and push, ending on the impact) and 4 (the recovery: held out, back to the carry idle), which the cook loads as it loads states 0 to 2. The states are known by their index, as the game reads them (the cook's states[0] take_time, states[2] put_time; the machine's order).",
